WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.810
Set a heap of flour alight,
and it only smoulders.

2
00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:08.810
Spread the same flour through the air
as a cloud of dust, and it can explode.

3
00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:11.210
Same flour, same air.

4
00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:12.730
So what's different?

5
00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:17.830
Why can a cloud of flour dust explode,
when a heap of flour only smoulders?

6
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.830
In this mission, you'll
meet collision theory:

7
00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.710
what has to happen when particles
collide for them to react.

8
00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:27.070
You'll find out how
temperature, concentration,

9
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:31.910
pressure and catalysts each
change the rate of a reaction.

10
00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:36.050
Your mission: explain why a
cloud of flour dust can explode.
